<body>
    <h1>Firm Onboarding</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <h1 id=3D"FirmOnboarding-BusinessContext">Business Context</h1>
<h1 id=3D"FirmOnboarding-BusinessRequirement">Business Requirement</h1>
<p><a href=3D"/spaces/NWPI/pages/1425647157/Firm+Management">Firm Managemen=
t</a></p>
<h1 id=3D"FirmOnboarding-Architecture">Architecture</h1>
<p>Supported Firm types</p>
<ul>
 <li>IB</li>
 <li>PM</li>
 <li>IFM</li>
 <li>Internal</li>
 <li><s>OT :warning:</s></li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"FirmOnboarding-Firmdataloading">Firm data loading</h2>
<p><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;"><em><strong>Unverified - Needs some POC f=
or validation</strong></em></span></p>
<p><a href=3D"/spaces/NA/pages/1336995931/Manage+Firm#ManageFirm-Architectu=
re">Manage Firm#Architecture</a></p>
<p>AWS step functions will be triggered from the data feed and initiate a w=
orkflow where each row will be processed independently for the use-cases be=
low.</p>
<p>Any exceptions will be flagged and would await user intervention to proc=
eed or skip further processing.<br>
  All auto or manually approved updates will be pushed to Firm configuratio=
n API via REST.</p>
<p>All updates will be processed asynchronously using kafka data topic and =
events will be emitted for successful updates. Unsuccessful updates will be=
 logged in Datadog and will raise alerts.</p>
<p>Events will be read by AWS workflow to mark the corresponding updates as=
 complete.</p>
<p>The Datadog alerts will prompt support to look into the issue and mark c=
orresponding updates manually to success/failure.</p>
<p><br></p>
<p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-manu=
al-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" heigh=
t=3D"247" src=3D"b97a87f505f9e49f0870b076787dd877207aa7a9af60a9e795a41d359c=
33713d" data-image-src=3D"/download/attachments/1230180648/image-2023-4-14_=
14-24-53.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1681496694039&amp;api=3Dv2"=
 data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"1477660387"=
 data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment=
" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image-2023-4-14_14-24-53.png" data-=
base-url=3D"https://wiki.bnc.ca" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image=
/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"1230180648" data-linked-resource=
-container-version=3D"17" tabindex=3D"0" alt=3D"" width=3D"468"></span></p>
<h2 id=3D"FirmOnboarding-FirmOnboardingUsecases">Firm Onboarding Use cases<=
/h2>
<h3 id=3D"FirmOnboarding-Creation">Creation</h3>
<ol>
 <li>Create a few firm=20
  <ol>
   <li>Create a new parent firm if needed</li>
  </ol></li>
</ol>
<h3 id=3D"FirmOnboarding-Update">Update</h3>
<p><em>Changes are detected by matching the FirmID from the source system</=
em></p>
<p><em>Events are sent for each of the below cases</em></p>
<h4 id=3D"FirmOnboarding-typechange">type change</h4>
<ol>
 <li>firm is active, raise an exception / break</li>
 <li>firm is inactive, update firm type</li>
</ol>
<h4 id=3D"FirmOnboarding-namechange">name change</h4>
<h4 id=3D"FirmOnboarding-FirmIDchange">Firm ID change</h4>
<ol>
 <li>Since, this is a new Firm ID, the RR range would conflict with the exi=
sting firm, thereby raising an exception.</li>
</ol>
<h4 id=3D"FirmOnboarding-RRrangeadded">RR range added</h4>
<ol>
 <li>If there's full/partial overlap of this range with an existing range, =
raise an exception</li>
 <li>Validate RR ranges and raise an exception for invalid ranges</li>
 <li>Auto-assign this range to users within this firm with firm scope user =
group assigned</li>
</ol>
<h4 id=3D"FirmOnboarding-RRrangeremoved">RR range removed</h4>
<ol>
 <li>remove the RR range</li>
</ol>
<h4 id=3D"FirmOnboarding-parentchange">parent change</h4>
<ol>
 <li>Create a new parent firm if this firm didn't have a parent and the par=
ent firm doesn't exist</li>
 <li>If this firm has another parent, raise an exception</li>
 <li>leave the firm type as null/empty</li>
</ol>
<h4 id=3D"FirmOnboarding-activation">activation</h4>
<ol>
 <li>activate the firm</li>
</ol>
<h3 id=3D"FirmOnboarding-Removal">Removal</h3>
<h4 id=3D"FirmOnboarding-de-activation">de-activation</h4>
<ol>
 <li>If the firm is already inactive, raise an exception</li>
 <li>de-activate the firm</li>
 <li>de-activate all child firms (if any)</li>
</ol>
<h4 id=3D"FirmOnboarding-Parentassociationchange">Parent association change=
</h4>
<ol>
 <li>Identify all firms without a firm type and parent ID</li>
 <li>Remove these firms</li>
</ol>
<h2 id=3D"FirmOnboarding-FirmConfigurationchanges">Firm Configuration chang=
es</h2>
<h4 id=3D"FirmOnboarding-typechange.1">type change</h4>
<ol>
 <li>trigger access control for firm package assignments and all associated=
 users&nbsp;</li>
</ol>
<h4 id=3D"FirmOnboarding-namechange.1">name change</h4>
<h4 id=3D"FirmOnboarding-RRrangeadded.1">RR range added</h4>
<ol>
 <li>Auto-assign this range to users within this firm with firm scope user =
group assigned</li>
</ol>
<h4 id=3D"FirmOnboarding-RRrangeremoved.1">RR range removed</h4>
<ol>
 <li>Un-assign this range to users within this firm with firm scope user gr=
oup assigned</li>
</ol>
<h4 id=3D"FirmOnboarding-activation.1">activation</h4>
<ol>
 <li>Activate firm configuration</li>
</ol>
<h3 id=3D"FirmOnboarding-Removal.1">Removal</h3>
<h4 id=3D"FirmOnboarding-de-activation.1">de-activation</h4>
<ol>
 <li>remove firm configuration</li>
 <li>remove all RR assignments and ranges</li>
 <li>de-activate all users of the firm and it's children (:question: link t=
o user management flow)</li>
</ol>
<p><br></p>
    </div>
</body>
